  "term": "environmental enrichment",
  "definition": "Environmental enrichment is a setting that adds social and nonliving stimulation to an organism’s surroundings. In the supplied source, it is described as increasing activity-related synaptic plasticity and improving behavior and memory, including reversing memory problems linked to social isolation.",
